 INPUT CARD>! needed because the hydrate (C2H5ClO2) and aldehyde (C2H3ClO) differ by a      
 INPUT CARD>! whole water molecule's worth of atoms -- their energies cannot be compared    
 INPUT CARD>! directly; the reactant side needs a separately computed water molecule        
 INPUT CARD>! added to balance the equation.                                                
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Starting geometry: extracted from the converged, confirmed-genuine-minimum    
 INPUT CARD>! "first" IRC-point cluster (caa005bIRCCML1st-prerelax-631Gdp.log), taking      
