 INPUT CARD>! analysis: C3=O4 at 1.213 A, a genuine carbonyl double bond, and C3-H12 the    
 INPUT CARD>! aldehyde's own CH proton) and discarding the two spectator water molecules.   
 INPUT CARD>! Since those waters are no longer present to hydrogen-bond to, this geometry   
 INPUT CARD>! will relax somewhat on re-optimization -- that is expected and correct.       
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
